        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Devil's Crush (known as Devil Crash in Japan) is a pinball video game developed by NAXAT Soft for the TurboGrafx-16 and released in 1990. The second installment in the Crush Pinball series after Alien Crush, the game has an eerie occult theme with skulls, skeletons, and demons. It was later followed by Jaki Crush and Alien Crush Returns.\n\nThe game was ported to the Sega Mega Drive, retitled Dragon's Fury (Devil Crash MD in Japan) which was developed by Technosoft. Devil's Crush was later released on the Wii's Virtual Console, with the European release reverting to its original title; however, the pentagram symbols were removed and replaced with 8-sided star.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Devil's Crush (conocido como Devil Crash en Japón) es un videojuego de pinball desarrollado por NAXAT Soft para TurboGrafx-16 y lanzado en 1990. Segunda entrega de la serie Crush Pinball tras Alien Crush, tiene una temática ocultista inquietante, con calaveras, esqueletos y demonios. Más tarde le siguieron Jaki Crush y Alien Crush Returns.\n\nEl juego se adaptó a Sega Mega Drive con el título Dragon's Fury (Devil Crash MD en Japón), desarrollado por Technosoft. Devil's Crush se lanzó después en la Consola Virtual de Wii; en la versión europea se recuperó el título original, pero los símbolos de pentagrama se eliminaron y se sustituyeron por una estrella de ocho lados.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "1990",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
